WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-23, with W6 (0.1.0)


STATE

  Version 0.1.0, Phase P2 start (expansions), on branch dev. It adds:
  - command substitution ($(...) and `...`), parsed once at parse time
    into TC_WPART_CMDSUB AST subtrees (including POSIX $((cmd); (cmd))
    disambiguation via tc_input_pushback, unquoted here-documents, and
    AST deep-cloning for functions);
  - $'...' ANSI-C quoting (POSIX.1-2024 XCU 2.2.4, including octal, hex,
    \u/\U UTF-8, \cX control escapes, and NUL truncation);
  - arithmetic expansion ($((...)), src/arith.c) with 64-bit signed
    integers, checked overflow, short-circuiting, and explicit recursion
    depth limit (128);
  - linear-time POSIX pattern matcher (src/pattern.c) with per-byte
    quoting metadata (no in-band escape bytes), wired into pathname
    expansion, case patterns, and ${x#pat}/${x##pat}/${x%pat}/${x%%pat};
  - IFS field splitting (POSIX XCU 2.6.5) and pathname expansion
    (src/glob.c, XCU 2.6.6 / 2.13.3).
  readelf -d lists only libc.so.6. make test and make sanitize pass.

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; lint mode is P2 0.1.5; tam-clam ships only its own key
  map (no built-in readline map), drafted in arch/keys.md and agreed with
  Fred before 0.2.0; FUNCNEST sets the function recursion limit; signed
  64-bit arithmetic overflow is a reported error.


